## 3. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE REVIEW

### Current Layer Reality

| Layer | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Routes | ✅ Exists (in main.py) | All routes functional |
| Schemas (Pydantic) | ⚠️ Inline | All 25+ models are defined inside main.py |
| Business Logic | ❌ Not separated | Business rules live inside route functions |
| Database Access | ❌ Not separated | Raw SQL executed inside every route |
| Services | ⚠️ Partially | Only `ai_mentor/` is extracted to services |
| Repository Layer | ❌ Missing | No data access abstraction |
| Middleware | ⚠️ Minimal | Only CORS; no request logging, rate limiting middleware |
| Config | ⚠️ Partial | JWT constants hardcoded; `dotenv` used for secrets |
| Models (ORM) | ❌ Missing | No SQLAlchemy ORM models — all raw SQL |

### Identified Architectural Issues

**Critical:**
- `run_migrations()` is called at module import (line 345). This means every `uvicorn` restart runs DDL against production database. There is no migration framework (Alembic).
- `failed_logins_tracker = {}` is an in-memory dict (line 759). It resets on every restart and does not work in multi-process or multi-instance deployments.
- DB sessions opened inside `get_current_user` dependency but not always properly closed (line 413–419).

**High:**
- All Pydantic schemas in main.py — makes the file enormous and harder to maintain.
- No ORM models — all `SELECT *` queries risk column-order regressions on schema changes.
- `db.close()` is in `finally` blocks (good) but the pattern is manual, not using FastAPI's dependency injection properly.

**Medium:**
- Two AI systems coexist: Gemini (`/api/v1/ai/chat`) and Groq (`/api/v1/mentor/chat`). There is duplication of large inline fallback response strings (~200 lines of hardcoded mock content).
- Helper functions (`create_notification`, `log_faculty_activity`, `log_audit`, `fetch_announcements_helper`) are defined inside main.py — they should be extracted to `backend/utils/`.

