## 6. DATABASE AUDIT

### Connection & Session

| Item | Status | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| `database.py` | ✅ Good | Validates PostgreSQL URI at startup |
| `pool_size=10, max_overflow=20` | ✅ Reasonable | For a team-scale app |
| `pool_pre_ping=True` | ✅ Good | Handles stale connections |
| `pool_recycle=300` | ✅ Good | 5-minute connection recycling |
| Manual `db.close()` in finally | ✅ Consistent | But not using FastAPI `Depends(get_db)` pattern |
| ORM models | ❌ None | All raw SQL — no SQLAlchemy declarative models |
| Migration tool | ❌ None | `run_migrations()` in main.py runs on every startup |

### Migration System Issues
`run_migrations()` (lines 40–344) runs **30+ `ALTER TABLE` and `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`** statements every time the application starts. This is:
- Slow on startup
- Risk of race conditions in multi-worker deployments
- Not tracked/versioned — no rollback possible
- **Fix:** Replace with Alembic migration framework.

### Query Patterns

| Pattern | Prevalence | Risk |
|---------|-----------|------|
| `SELECT *` queries | ~15 occurrences | Schema change regressions |
| Repeated identical queries | High | `institution_id` lookups repeated in every endpoint |
| No query pagination (some endpoints) | Several | Memory risk on large datasets |
| Hardcoded schema defaults | Several | e.g., `institution_id = 1` as fallback |
| Missing indexes | Some tables | `token_blacklist` indexed on `token` (PK) — good |

