## 7. AI MODULE AUDIT

### Two AI Systems Currently Running

#### System A — Groq (Primary, `/api/v1/mentor/*`)
- Files: `backend/services/ai_mentor/`
- Provider: Groq (LLaMA-based)
- Session management: ✅ DB-backed chat sessions
- Memory: ✅ `memory_service.py` with rolling context
- Prompt builder: ✅ `prompt_builder.py` with context
- Streaming: ✅ Supported via `/api/v1/mentor/chat`
- Error handling: ⚠️ Basic — bare `try/except`

#### System B — Gemini (Legacy, `/api/v1/ai/chat`)
- Location: Inside `main.py` (~500 lines)
- Provider: Google Gemini
- Session management: ❌ None — single `mentor_messages` table
- Memory: ⚠️ Last 6 messages only, no session isolation
- Streaming: ✅ `/api/v1/ai/chat/stream` endpoint exists
- Fallback responses: 🔴 200+ lines of hardcoded mock text inside main.py

**Recommendation:** System A (Groq) is the superior architecture. System B (Gemini) should be deprecated and removed after validating that all frontend consumers use the Groq endpoints.

### AI Wellness Module
- Uses Gemini to generate wellness recommendations
- Gracefully falls back to rule-based recommendations if Gemini unavailable
- ✅ Good fallback pattern

